msgstr "Enter port counts in verified DSM controller order, separated by commas (example: 4,2). Each count must be 1 through 9. Loader detection does not establish DSM order or physical bay mapping. A candidate is shown before confirmation."

#: MSGZZ217
msgid "Invalid port counts or maxdisks limit. Enter comma-separated numbers from 1 through 9 whose sum does not exceed maxdisks."
msgstr "Invalid port counts or maxdisks limit. Enter comma-separated numbers from 1 through 9 whose sum does not exceed maxdisks."

#: MSGZZ218
msgid "Candidate only - not verified or applied"
msgstr "Candidate only - not verified or applied"

#: MSGZZ219
msgid "No valid maxdisks value exists in user_config.json. No candidate was calculated."
msgstr "No valid maxdisks value exists in user_config.json. No candidate was calculated."

#: MSGZZ220
msgid "The mapping calculator is missing. Update the complete MSHELL bundle."
msgstr "The mapping calculator is missing. Update the complete MSHELL bundle."

#: MSGZZ221
msgid "SataPortMap or DiskIdxMap is already configured. Adding sata_remap can make disk ordering harder to predict. Existing values will not be removed. Continue?"
msgstr "SataPortMap or DiskIdxMap is already configured. Adding sata_remap can make disk ordering harder to predict. Existing values will not be removed. Continue?"

#: MSGZZ222
msgid "This candidate is not verified against DSM disk order. Apply it? A loader rebuild is not required when booting DSM through FRIEND."
msgstr "This candidate is not verified against DSM disk order. Apply it? A loader rebuild is not required when booting DSM through FRIEND."

#: MSGZZ223
msgid "Cannot apply this mapping: check maxdisks and remove any conflicting sata_remap first."
msgstr "Cannot apply this mapping: check maxdisks and remove any conflicting sata_remap first."

#: MSGZZ224
msgid "No valid previous mapping backup is available."
msgstr "No valid previous mapping backup is available."

#: MSGZZ225
msgid "The mapping could not be saved or validated. The previous configuration was restored."
msgstr "The mapping could not be saved or validated. The previous configuration was restored."

#: MSGZZ226
msgid "Restore the previous SATA mapping? A loader rebuild is not required when booting DSM through FRIEND."
msgstr "Restore the previous SATA mapping? A loader rebuild is not required when booting DSM through FRIEND."

#: MSGZZ227
msgid "Enter a verified DSM disk-index permutation, for example 0>4:4>0. Loader host and ATA numbers do not prove DSM disk order. Cancel to leave settings unchanged."
msgstr "Enter a verified DSM disk-index permutation, for example 0>4:4>0. Loader host and ATA numbers do not prove DSM disk order. Cancel to leave settings unchanged."

#: MSGZZ228
msgid "Invalid mapping. Use unique indices 0 through 255 and a complete permutation, for example 0>4:4>0. No setting was changed."
msgstr "Invalid mapping. Use unique indices 0 through 255 and a complete permutation, for example 0>4:4>0. No setting was changed."

#: MSGZZ229
msgid "These disk indices must be verified in DSM. Applying the wrong mapping may change disk order. Save? A loader rebuild is not required when booting DSM through FRIEND."
msgstr "These disk indices must be verified in DSM. Applying the wrong mapping may change disk order. Save? A loader rebuild is not required when booting DSM through FRIEND."

#: MSGZZ230
msgid "Choose how to prepare SATA disk-index remapping"
msgstr "Choose how to prepare SATA disk-index remapping"

#: MSGZZ231
msgid "Generate candidate from verified disk indices"
msgstr "Generate candidate from verified disk indices"

#: MSGZZ232
msgid "Enter mapping manually"
msgstr "Enter mapping manually"

#: MSGZZ233
msgid "Enter verified DSM disk indices in disk order, separated by commas, for example 0,1,2,3,4. Use the original indices without sata_remap; loader device numbers are not DSM indices."
msgstr "Enter verified DSM disk indices in disk order, separated by commas, for example 0,1,2,3,4. Use the original indices without sata_remap; loader device numbers are not DSM indices."

#: MSGZZ234
msgid "Enter the desired index for each disk in the same order, for example 4,1,2,3,0. Use the same set of indices exactly once."
msgstr "Enter the desired index for each disk in the same order, for example 4,1,2,3,0. Use the same set of indices exactly once."

#: MSGZZ235
msgid "An existing sata_remap is configured. Its current DSM indices may already be remapped. Remove it and verify the original DSM indices before generating a new candidate. No settings were changed."
msgstr "An existing sata_remap is configured. Its current DSM indices may already be remapped. Remove it and verify the original DSM indices before generating a new candidate. No settings were changed."

#: MSGZZ236
msgid "Cannot generate a mapping. Both lists must contain the same unique indices from 0 through 255, and at least one index must change."
msgstr "Cannot generate a mapping. Both lists must contain the same unique indices from 0 through 255, and at least one index must change."

